{{TAGS trench ai}}

**TL;DR**: One of the best tips to improve quality _and_ reduce token
consumption when writing software with AI is to keep your `AGENTS.md` (or its
equivalent) up to date.

---

I have flown back into Malta, after a week of training multiple software teams
in Georgia (the country, not the state) about generative AI and I am, as usual,
swamped with the amazing amount of advances and research coming in from all
directions.  I typically share these thoughts on LinkedIn, but [my friend Andrew
Sundstrom basically said, "knock it
off."](https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7519791516786151424?commentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A%28activity%3A7519791516786151424%2C7519867121263173632%29&dashCommentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Afsd_comment%3A%287519867121263173632%2Curn%3Ali%3Aactivity%3A7519791516786151424%29).
I should be writing stuff here, where it's easier to find.

